+                     * changed (a fresh cuMemAlloc leaf mapped, or a freed one scrubbed).  Arm a
+                     * re-sweep so the NEXT doorbell re-walks and backs the newly-mapped leaves
+                     * into the host GR VAS BEFORE the GR channel's CE touches them.  Without
+                     * this, the dirty flag (set only on writes to ALREADY-tracked PT pages) miss
+                     * a mapping whose PTE lands on a PT page allocated since the last sweep, so
+                     * the last buffer leaf is left unbacked and the host GR CE FAULT_PDEs on it
+                     * one 2 MiB page past the last-backed gpga (#13: cup8_iter N=1536 iter-2).
+                     * Idle in steady-state compute (no allocation => CeUtils quiet) => no LLM
+                     * perf regression; fires during the alloc/free churn where a sweep is due. */
+                    if (!nvkvm_m2_is_user_ce(s, s->chan_client) &&
